        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: DIVA, Cleo, Paper Giants: The Birth of Cleo\n- People: Charlotte Cooper, Ita Buttrose\n- Organizations: Disability and Society, Fat Studies: An Interdisciplinary Journal of Body Weight and Society, The Guardian\n- Places: United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand\n\nFacts:\n- Cleo was founded in Australia in 1972.\n- Paper Giants: The Birth of Cleo is a 2011 Australian two-part television miniseries about the beginning of Cleo magazine and its creator, Ita Buttrose.\n- The Australia and New Zealand editions of Cleo were discontinued in 2016.\n- DIVA is a leading lesbian magazine in the United Kingdom and is published monthly.\n- Charlotte Cooper has published articles in the academic journal Disability and Society.\n- Charlotte Cooper is a board member of Fat Studies: An Interdisciplinary Journal of Body Weight and Society.\n- Charlotte Cooper has written many articles on fat acceptance and gay rights for websites, magazines, and newspapers, including Diva and The Guardian.",
